cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "textblast: text reuse detection with a patched NCBI BLAST engine"
version: 0.9.0
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23729155
repository-code: "https://github.com/Solemne-ERC/textblast"
abstract: >-
  textblast detects text reuse in historical document collections. It normalizes and encodes texts as protein-like
  sequences, aligns them with NCBI BLAST+ patched for text (a uniform match/mismatch matrix and matching gap costs),
  and maps every hit back to exact character offsets of the input. It then joins, defragments, annotates, filters and
  clusters the hits, and exports tables and formats for analysis. It works on any collection of texts in the Latin
  script, given as JSON Lines.
authors:
  - family-names: Schmidt
    given-names: Gleb
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6925-551X"
    affiliation: "Radboud University, Faculty of Arts, Humanities Lab"
keywords:
  - text reuse
  - intertextuality
  - textual relatedness
  - sequence alignment
  - BLAST
  - historical texts
  - Latin
  - digital humanities
  - computational philology
